From: Tactipalm <local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h618: enable display on OrangePi Zero 2W

Armbian's sunxi-6.18 patches.drm series adds the DE33 display pipeline to the
H616/H618 SoC, but its board-enablement patch (0042) does not cover the
OrangePi Zero 2W.

The sibling boards get their enablement in two places. The Zero 2 and Zero 3
board files only add &hdmi, because they include sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
which supplies the connector node, &de and &hdmi_out. The Zero 2W includes
sun50i-h616.dtsi directly, so it inherits none of that and needs all four
pieces here:

  - an hdmi-connector node with an endpoint
  - &de status okay          (display-engine defaults to disabled in the dtsi)
  - &hdmi with its supply    (aldo1 is vcc1v8, as on the Zero 3)
  - &hdmi_out endpoint       (links the encoder to the connector)

Enabling &hdmi alone is not enough: the display-engine node stays disabled, so
sun4i-drm never binds and no DRM device appears.

The connector is typed "c" (mini-HDMI) rather than the "d" (micro-HDMI) used by
the Zero 2/Zero 3 dtsi, matching the socket actually fitted to this board.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
@@ -24,6 +24,17 @@
 		stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8";
 	};
 
+	connector {
+		compatible = "hdmi-connector";
+		type = "c";		/* the Zero 2W carries a mini-HDMI socket */
+
+		port {
+			hdmi_con_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_out_con>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	leds {
 		compatible = "gpio-leds";
 
@@ -63,6 +74,10 @@
 	cpu-supply = <&reg_dcdc2>;
 };
 
+&de {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &ehci1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -74,6 +89,17 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&hdmi {
+	hvcc-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&hdmi_out {
+	hdmi_out_con: endpoint {
+		remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_con_in>;
+	};
+};
+
 &mmc0 {
 	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PF6 */
 	bus-width = <4>;
